@spec mm_take_window_spec  src=tests/specs/mm_take_window_spec.lua  loc=79  cases=3
@exercises midiManager (h.mm)
@surface   mm:load, mm:setLength, mm:length, mm:resolution, mm:timeSigs
@harness   fakeReaper:setTempo, fakeReaper:bindTake, fakeReaper.SetMediaItemInfo_Value, fakeReaper.SetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value, fakeReaper:seedMidi, fakeReaper.GetMediaItemInfo_Value, fakeReaper:addTimeSigMarker

# Intent
  Integration spec: real midiManager + fakeReaper. Pins mm's length and
  time-signature reads to the source rather than the item. A head-trimmed
  instance starts inside its source, and tm's ppq frame runs from the source
  origin, so anything measured from D_POSITION is out by the head.
  See docs/arrangeManager.md § The take's window.

# Helpers
  @fn headTrimmed(headQN, sourceQN, renderedQN)  @ 14-27
      -- The shape am:trimHead leaves: the item start walked headQN forward with
      -- D_STARTOFFS to match, so source ppq 0 sits headQN before the item.
      -- Tempo 60 makes the fake's seconds and QN agree across both time frames.
  @fn itemRange(fakeReaper, item)  @ 29-32

# Cases
  @case 'setLength sizes the source from its origin: the item ends head QN sooner'  [pure]  @ 36-46
  @case 'a source shrunk inside the head leaves a zero-length item, never a backwards one'  [pure]  @ 49-58
  @case 'timeSigs spans the whole source, so markers in the head and past the end land'  [pure]  @ 61-77

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call mm:load  @ 25
  @use call mm:setLength  @ 40,53
  @use call mm:length  @ 45
  @use call mm:resolution  @ 45,70
  @use call mm:timeSigs  @ 69

# Fields (r read / w write incl. constructor keys)
  @field w ccs  @ 23
  @field w denom  @ 73,74,75,76
  @field w name  @ 36,49,61
  @field w num  @ 73,74,75,76
  @field w ppq  @ 73,74,75,76
